# 64-atom SiC zinc-blende crystal under the Tersoff bond-order potential,
# constrained to the C_2(z) subgroup of the full F-43m point group by
# fix symmetry. Demonstrates fix symmetry on a real materials-science
# setup: chemically distinct atom types, 3-body bond-order forces, and a
# non-trivial 2-fold rotation that pins Si atoms on the rotation axis
# while leaving C atoms paired across z.
#
# Zinc-blende SiC has no inversion symmetry (inversion swaps Si and C),
# so P-1 cannot be used. The 2-fold rotation about z preserves both FCC
# sublattices, hence both atom types.
#
# Companion files data.sic_c2 and sic_c2.json are produced by
# generate_sic_c2.py.

units           metal
atom_style      atomic
boundary        p p p
atom_modify     map array

read_data       data.sic_c2
Reading data file ...
  orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (8.72 8.72 8.72)
  2 by 1 by 2 MPI processor grid
  reading atoms ...
  64 atoms
  read_data CPU = 0.001 seconds

# SiC.tersoff lists C first, then Si. data.sic_c2 sets type 1 = C, type 2 = Si.
pair_style      tersoff
pair_coeff      * * SiC.tersoff C Si
Reading tersoff potential file SiC.tersoff with DATE: 2011-04-26

# Small thermal kick so the dynamics is non-trivial. The 2-fold rotation
# constrains Si atoms on the corner sublattice to move only along z.
velocity        all create 300.0 87287 mom yes rot yes

fix             1 all nve
fix             sym all symmetry sic_c2.json

timestep        0.0005
thermo          50
thermo_style    custom step temp pe etotal press

# Pick representative orbits from sic_c2.json:
#   tag 1  Wyckoff Si on the rotation axis at (0,0,0)   -> x = y = 0 forever
#   tags 5  & 32  paired C atoms                         -> sum_xy/L is integer, z equal
#   tags 2  & 18  paired Si atoms                        -> same invariants
variable        wy_x   equal x[1]
variable        wy_y   equal y[1]
variable        c_resx equal (x[5]+x[32])/lx-round((x[5]+x[32])/lx)
variable        c_resy equal (y[5]+y[32])/ly-round((y[5]+y[32])/ly)
variable        c_dz   equal z[5]-z[32]
variable        si_resx equal (x[2]+x[18])/lx-round((x[2]+x[18])/lx)
variable        si_resy equal (y[2]+y[18])/ly-round((y[2]+y[18])/ly)
variable        si_dz   equal z[2]-z[18]

print           "pre-run  Wyckoff Si: (${wy_x},${wy_y})  C pair: res=(${c_resx},${c_resy}) dz=${c_dz}  Si pair: res=(${si_resx},${si_resy}) dz=${si_dz}"
pre-run  Wyckoff Si: (0,0)  C pair: res=(0,0) dz=0  Si pair: res=(0,0) dz=0
run             200

